Original commit body from d81de97dc959a3660cb76023f01062de0f3f2f56:

tests/test_backfill_training_data_cohort_tags.py intermittently failed five
tests at once on subprocess.TimeoutExpired, all from one command:

    git log --pretty=format:'%aI %H' --reverse -- <one path>

MEASURED IN CI by a purpose-built probe, same step, seconds apart:

    run1: elapsed_ms=1185559   (19m46s)
    run2: elapsed_ms=19
    post: elapsed_ms=27        (after the whole suite)

run2 is a FRESH git process, so the expense is I/O -- reading the pack -- not
computation. With --reverse plus a pathspec over 6,445 commits, no commit-graph
(fresh clone) and 7 packs, git reads essentially the whole object store. It is
the ONLY full-history walk in the suite, so it alone pays that cold cost, every
run, inside a 30s cap.

FIX, two halves:
  - prepare-git runs `git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths` in
    BOTH workflows that execute the root tests/ tree (per-PR gate + full-suite;
    nightly runs packages/*/tests/ only). Absorbs the cold read outside any
    timeout AND leaves changed-path Bloom filters so the walk is structurally
    cheap. Local: walk 0.044s -> build 0.268s -> walk 0.010s.
  - the five tests share a class-scoped `timeline` fixture instead of
    recomputing the identical walk five times -- which is what turned one slow
    command into five red tests and burned 5 x 30s before failing.

BOUNDED (300s) AND NON-FATAL ON PURPOSE. The 1,185s was measured while four
nightly matrix legs competed for the same disk, so the cold read is unbounded
and load-dependent; relocating an unbounded cost into every pipeline would
trade a flaky test for a slow one. On timeout we are exactly where we were --
and the reading it did still warmed the cache.

Eight hypotheses died by measurement before this one: runner starvation (CI ran
the suite FASTER than the dev box, 359s vs 572s), shallow history, missing
commit-graph alone (0.095s forced cold), over-parallelism (-n 8), fresh-clone
and shallow-then-unshallow repo states (0.026s / 0.041s), a gitattributes
textconv driver, and auto-gc.

Probe trimmed to the three timing lines as a regression guard; GIT_TRACE2_PERF
removed (359,742 lines for no payoff, and its kill-detection summary was wrong
-- trace2 repeats the command line only on `start`, so an `exit` can never
match a command-line grep).

NOTE ON LANDING: auto-pr will hit WI-ninar on this PR (poll_ci declares "hung
runner" on every pipeline over 300s on this backend), so it is pushed with
CI_STALE_PENDING_SECONDS raised. That is a workaround, not a fix; WI-ninar is.

